{"uid":"1e2df65e64e271c1","name":"test_wave_scoped_ruling_reaches_the_peer_verdict_gate_after_a_replan","fullName":"tests.test_operator_ruling#test_wave_scoped_ruling_reaches_the_peer_verdict_gate_after_a_replan","historyId":"e41f63e29c09fb367d783d88d14979cd","time":{"start":1791957926519,"stop":1791957926528,"duration":9},"description":"D.8's OTHER judging hat (task 018, #196): the peer verdict gate can\n    reject a finished approach on its own, so a wave-scoped ruling has to\n    render binding in the gate's prompt too -- otherwise the gate rejects a\n    run over exactly the obligation the operator already ruled on, which is\n    the shape #196 reports.\n\n    Drives the REAL `_step_verdict_gate` with the REAL `run_iteration`\n    spied on (so a renamed keyword cannot hide a regression the way a\n    source-inspection check would), after the same replan\n    `test_wave_scoped_ruling_survives_a_replan_and_stays_binding` simulates:\n    approach bumped to 2 and a plan whose ids name a different task. Then\n    renders what the hat is actually handed, `build_prompt('verdict_gate',\n    extra=...)`.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>D.8's OTHER judging hat (task 018, #196): the peer verdict gate can<br />\nreject a finished approach on its own, so a wave-scoped ruling has to<br />\nrender binding in the gate's prompt too -- otherwise the gate rejects a<br />\nrun over exactly the obligation the operator already ruled on, which is<br />\nthe shape #196 reports.</p>\n<pre><code>Drives the REAL `_step_verdict_gate` with the REAL `run_iteration`\nspied on (so a renamed keyword cannot hide a regression the way a\nsource-inspection check would), after the same replan\n`test_wave_scoped_ruling_survives_a_replan_and_stays_binding` simulates:\napproach bumped to 2 and a plan whose ids name a different task. Then\nrenders what the hat is actually handed, `build_prompt('verdict_gate',\nextra=...)`.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":fals